.0.0-beta", "expected_failure_match": true, "failure": "test_less_than panicked: matched 1.0.0-beta", "fixed_commit": "5742fc2f584dc14b46199d797de65305fe9b5144", "fixed_tree": "d2daade0f7ba35fc2705b439ce3b96d20ab84477", "fixes": [{"commit": "5742fc2f584dc14b46199d797de65305fe9b5144", "parent": "35d918d334cdecc9725e217f460b90f478b5dabd"}], "patch": "patches/5742fc2f584dc14b46199d797de65305fe9b5144-1/20260924T005132Z-b911e2e4.patch", "provenance": "verbatim", "restored_source_matches": true, "runs": {"buggy": {"exit_code": 101, "log": "evidence/5742fc2f584dc14b46199d797de65305fe9b5144-1/20260924T005132Z-b911e2e4/buggy.log", "named_result": "FAILED", "tests_run": 1, "timed_out": false}, "fixed": {"exit_code": 0, "log": "evidence/5742fc2f584dc14b46199d797de65305fe9b5144-1/20260924T005132Z-b911e2e4/fixed.log", "named_result": "ok", "tests_run": 1, "timed_out": false}, "restored": {"exit_code": 0, "log": "evidence/5742fc2f584dc14b46199d797de65305fe9b5144-1/20260924T005132Z-b911e2e4/restored.log", "named_result": "ok", "tests_run": 1, "timed_out": false}}, "signature": "matched 1.0.0-beta", "test_sources": [{"commit": "5742fc2f584dc14b46199d797de65305fe9b5144", "paths": ["src/eval.rs"]}], "tests": ["test_less_than"]}, "shard": "semver", "status": "confirmed", "subject": "Fix <I.J to not match I.J.0 prereleases", "summary": "The old Less branch incorrectly accepts 1.0.0-beta for >1.0.0-alpha, <1.0: both matches_exact and matches_greater return false for the patch-less upper bound, so their negated conjunction returns true. The fix uses matches_less, which rejects matching major/minor versions when the comparator omits its patch. Existing test_less_than in tests/test_version_req.rs explicitly rejects this case and the analogous <1 case. The proposed reversal restores only the Less branch. No tests were executed.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T00:52:43.444813+00:00"}
{"commit": "a5850bbd0d1bf6e5ae1ed1310cbe8919fa77d618", "id": "a5850bbd0d1bf6e5ae1ed1310cbe8919fa77d618-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Proposal names no upstream test", "repo": "https://github.com/dtolnay/semver", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260924T005657Z-2058d30e", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/a5850bbd0d1bf6e5ae1ed1310cbe8919fa77d618-1/20260924T005657Z-2058d30e/origin.json": "b70aba043c6e2bac860de926b4deb489370aaffec1eb026608551b4a5685ccb6", "evidence/a5850bbd0d1bf6e5ae1ed1310cbe8919fa77d618-1/20260924T005657Z-2058d30e/proposal.json": "6261e35299572ff0a96d9ba719a7cbc696c315eb3e9eb233f178aedd0545429d"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "semver", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Disallow patch version digit after minor version wildcard", "summary": "The parser's `UnexpectedAfterWildcard` guard gated on `op == Op::Wildcard`, so when an explicit operator preceded the wildcard (e.g. `>1.*.0`) the guard never fired and the parser silently accepted a concrete patch digit after a minor wildcard.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T00:56:57.760236+00:00"}
